com/repos/python/mypy/labels/topic-typed-dict","name":"topic-typed-dict","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2022-09-28T16:11:36Z","updated_at":"2022-09-28T22:14:41Z","closed_at":"2022-09-28T22:11:18Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Bug Report**\r\n\r\nWhen pulling the example of Generics from the [documentation](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/generics.html) and specifying a generic TypedDict following the [blog post](https://mypy-lang.blogspot.com/2022/09/mypy-0981-released.html), I get an error on simple Generic example.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import Generic, TypeVar\r\nfrom typing_extensions import TypedDict  # I am using python 3.10.4\r\n\r\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\r\nMyDict = TypedDict(\"MyDict\", {\"foo\": T})\r\n\r\nclass Stack(Generic[T]):  # mypy error: Free type variable expected in Generic[...]  [misc]\r\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\r\n        pass\r\n```\r\nCommenting line 5 removes the error. Moving line 5 after the declaration of `Stack` also works.\r\n\r\n**Expected Behavior**\r\nThat class Stack is a correct Generic and mypy should not error.\r\n\r\n**Your Environment**\r\n- Mypy version used: 0.981\r\n- Python version used: 3.10.4","closed_by":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkiv